To simplify $\frac{5+7i}{2-3i}$, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:
\[
\frac{5+7i}{2-3i} \cdot \frac{2+3i}{2+3i} = \frac{(5+7i)(2+3i)}{(2-3i)(2+3i)}
\]
Expanding both the numerator and the denominator:
\[
= \frac{5 \cdot 2 + 5 \cdot 3i + 7i \cdot 2 + 7i \cdot 3i}{2^2 - (3i)^2}
= \frac{10 + 15i + 14i + 21i^2}{4 + 9}
= \frac{10 + 29i - 21}{13}
= \frac{-11 + 29i}{13}
\]
Separating the real and imaginary parts:
\[
= \frac{-11}{13} + \frac{29}{13}i = \boxed{\dfrac{-11}{13} + \dfrac{29}{13}i}
\]

